itch handling for station') Signed-off-by: Cathy Luo &lt;cluo@marvell.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Kalle Valo &lt;kvalo@codeaurora.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit a6139b6271f9f95377fe3486aed6120c9142779b  git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/kvalo/wireless-drivers-next.git  master) [backport due to directory change] Signed-off-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@google.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47848 TEST=`emerge-veyron_jerry chromeos-kernel-3_14`  Change-Id: Id5e5d2f4fd3dfacd315bfc9c6ab479ece93285be Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/348331 Commit-Ready: Amitkumar Karwar &lt;akarwar@marvell.com&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Amitkumar Karwar &lt;akarwar@marvell.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="348331" owner_email="akarwar@marvell.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/31/348331/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie7f2c60cc70ef1dea279af27b408d39189b45d7e" commit="e9c222fc83e75064e9afc53ddafbc5153aa4f99d" commit_message="sys-apps/upstart: backport socket event feature from 1.3  We want to utilize 'start on socket ...' events for CUPS.  Provide our own .conf instead of the example .conf, so we actually start with the rest of our boot services.  BUG=chromium:616778 TEST=write upstart script with 'start on socket ...' line, then try to      connect to that socket TEST=check `status upstart-socket-bridge` at boot  Change-Id: Ie7f2c60cc70ef1dea279af27b408d39189b45d7e Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/343270 Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="343270" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromium